.TH GROK-TUI-SHELL 1 "2026" "grok-bot-tui 0.7.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grok-tui-shell, grok-bot-tui \- companion TUI for Grok Bot (not Grok)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grok-tui-shell
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fItui\fR | \fIversion\fR | \fIwhoami\fR | \fIbots\fR | \fIstatus\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B grok-tui-shell
is a lightweight terminal client for
.B Grok Bot
(the Electron desktop app). It is
.B not
Grok, not grok.com chat, and not the official
.B grok
CLI.
.PP
Interactive mode (default
.BR tui )
needs a TTY. On Raspberry Pi, run it in a terminal, over SSH, or inside
.B tmux
(see AUTO-START).
.PP
Sign-in uses the same session as Grok Bot (complete it in the grok-bot window).
The TUI does not read Cookies and does not call
.B grok login
.BR .
Electron grok-bot is x86_64 only; the TUI itself runs on x86_64, aarch64, and
armv7l (Raspberry Pi 3/4/5).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Fullscreen TUI (default). Chat stays in this terminal.
.TP
.B chat
Send one message on stdout using the Grok Bot session. Never launches a GUI.
.TP
.B version
Print version.
.TP
.B whoami
Print signed-in label or "signed out". Exit 1 if signed out.
.TP
.B bots
List bots from the signed-in Grok Bot roster cache.
.TP
.B status
Arch, Python, desktop availability, signed-in, bot count.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
JSON for version/whoami/bots/status.
.TP
.B \-\-api-key \fIKEY\fR
Optional api.x.ai key (or XAI_API_KEY). Not Grok Bot SSO.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIID\fR
.TP
.B \-\-base-url \fIURL\fR
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
.TP
.B \-\-help
.SH TUI KEYS
.B /login
launch grok-bot + Cursor onboarding.
.B /agents
refresh roster.
.B j/k
move.
.B Enter
select.
.B Esc
or
.B ←
leave chat for the bot list.
.B /back
same as Esc from compose.
.B /gui
launch desktop (x86_64).
.B /quit
exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/grok-bot-tui/config.json
Non-secret defaults (model, timeout, base_url).
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/grok-tui-shell/credentials
Optional API key, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/Grok Bot/sand-client-persistence/
Grok Bot roster cache (read names only; never Cookies).
.SH AUTO-START
User systemd unit
.B grok-tui-shell.service
starts a tmux session named
.BR grok-tui .
On a headless Raspberry Pi:
.PP
.nf
loginctl enable-linger "$USER"
systemctl --user enable --now grok-tui-shell.service
tmux attach -t grok-tui
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
README in the grok-bot-tui package.
.SH NOTES
This is not Grok.
